        {
            "number": 10,
            "revision": "9e14b4bf335d6af2b94377e531e97543b5b2b731",
            "parents": [
                "64fe8020cfd6f2b6fb25249cc42daa9550c595b9"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/14/87114/10",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Ed Tanous",
                "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                "username": "edtanous"
            },
            "createdOn": 1770138434,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ed Tanous",
                "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                "username": "edtanous"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "since bmcweb has it's own logging functions, does it make sense to make a special one which prints under the condition that something like `--verbose` is passed to the bmcweb commandline?\n\nSomething like `BMCWEB_LOG_VERBOSE`\n\nHaving such a facility would avoid creating bit rot here and solve the use-case of 'we have logs which are seldom useful'\n\nOtherwise a meson option or the old `static bool debug` could also solve it without hiding this code from parsing + typechecking stage."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not really interested in supporting such a CLI argument.  The problem of bit rot in these doesn't seem like it will be much of an issue in practice if they're commented out.\n\nIf we want to have some kind of per-subsystem logging, that's something we should look at holistically, but I'm not that interested in it.  99% of the time I turn on the max log level to debug an issue, or promote a suspected log statement up to ERROR.  It's relatively rare that there are so many log statements that I need to drop the verbosity down.\n\nIf your or other peoples experience differ, I'm happy to have that discussion;  I'm not interested in implementing something complex for this here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "i did not try it, but what about an\n\n```\nif constexpr (false) {\n\tBMCWEB_LOG_DEBUG(\"...\");\n}\n```\n\n, that would rot less and not much effort to implement.\n\nIt's local to a function and does not need any extra symbol. Also relatively easy to grep for when someone needs to enable these logs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "with that each log ends up with 5 lines instead of 1 or 2.  If that's the tradeoff we're debating, I'll just delete these log statements.  That's easier."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Wouldn't `BMCWEB_LOG_VERBOSE` solve both the bit rot and the code size issue?\n\nIs it really so much work to introduce that extra function.\n\nAt least then there would be a single place to patch to enable all these logs.\nAnd then later someone could spin it into a meson option / CLI argument.\n\nIf they are not useful then perhaps just delete them. But commenting out does not seem like the right solution to me."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> Wouldn't BMCWEB_LOG_VERBOSE solve both the bit rot and the code size issue?\n\nAt the expense of having yet another log level, when the majority of people use Error, info, or debug.  If you want to try to go push for a new log level, that's something we can discuss in another MR (I'd probably still be against it).\n\nFor this MR, these have been commented out in the past in the same way I'm doing here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "i don't think this should go in like this.\n\nLet's just implement it properly to be able to enable these logs without applying patches."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> Let's just implement it properly \n\nIf \"properly\" means adding yet another logging level, that's not something I'm interested in taking the time to go define how we'd use.  This patchset doesn't preclude someone from doing that if they choose to in the future, and this patch as written solves the problem.\n\nWith respect, I suspect we need to agree to disagree here.  If adding a new level is something you'd like to see happen, please start a discussion (ideally starting with the docs change to define it) and we can go from there.\n\nLong term, if I'm going to apply effort to logging, it'll be to add something like open telemetry, but that's also a larger change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
